From bcb622bb15e47689d2f566dc61bb8c15341022b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:17:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): batch exact history reads on short-lived
 snapshots [daveey]

Task-only P2 invalidations with unchanged event count/max executed one exact
history SELECT per displayed task. Batch only those ambiguous comparisons;
retain count/max shortcuts, ordered storage-type/column parity and overlays.
Keep the existing observer only as a commit clock; close the guarded row
snapshot before projection, also on errors. No whole-payload cache or polling.

Proof:
- RED title-only edit: six per-task history SELECTs; GREEN one IN query.
- Real default shadow board copy, 189 displayed cards, migrated offline to
  install P2 triggers. Old/new serialized payload bytes match with fixed clock.
  Stable title-change SQL statements 242 -> 54; event reads 188 -> 1.
  Seven-request sequential-arm CPU medians 272.15ms -> 294.92ms (thread CPU).
  This bounds query/connection lifetime; it is not a demonstrated CPU speedup.
  Cold 624.85ms -> 731.93ms; unchanged 10.34ms -> 12.12ms; no live serve signals.
- 570 consumer tests pass across 36 files, plus 23 final focused tests.
- Reader-lifetime RED on original board_rows; success, failure/retry, unchanged
  and interleaved-clock/read commit regressions covered.
- Full scripts/check --base origin/main passes.

